# Weekly secret audit of $HOME critical paths (dotfiles, ~/bin, ~/repos,
# AI session logs). scan-for-secrets exits 2 on durable findings, which
# counts as a job failure here on purpose: it triggers the failure
# notification (macOS banner + ntfy push) so leaks reach your phone.
# Agent-scratchpad hits are reported but exit 0 — they are session-local
# tmp that self-clears, and repeatedly paged as false leaks (2026-08-25)
# before the scanner learned to classify them as transient.
# ~/.codex/shell_snapshots joined that class for the same reason: codex
# rewrites it on every session start, so it is a cache of the shell env and
# not a record of anything. Still printed, never paged on (sd:1254).
#
# This alarm is EXPECTED to keep firing. The findings it pages on are the
# key values inside the agent transcripts, and the operator accepted those
# rather than rotating them (local-scan-for-secrets/README.md, "Accepted
# exposure"). The retention prune that runs nightly addresses accumulation,
# not this finding — over 99% of the transcripts are under 30 days old and
# nothing is older than 90, so no window reaches the exposed material.
# Silencing the Monday page needs `mask --apply` or a decision to classify
# session logs the way scratchpads are classified; neither is done here.
# Output in logs/secret-scan-weekly.log.
JOB_SCHEDULE="0 7 * * 1"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-scan-for-secrets/scan-for-secrets.sh\" critical"
